{"uid":"338631a742e01adc","name":"test_python_code_node_falls_back_to_default_cap_without_config","fullName":"tests.test_workflow_runtime#test_python_code_node_falls_back_to_default_cap_without_config","historyId":"d29a91745a273296a8aedb4f8e495762","time":{"start":1789447681254,"stop":1789447681338,"duration":84},"description":"With no cap threaded onto the plan (preview / eval-replay paths), the sandbox\n    applies its class default.\n\n    This previously asserted that the node *failed* on a >64 KB output — because the\n    oversized value truncated the runner's JSON envelope. That was the C8 bounding\n    defect, not intended behaviour: the child now bounds its own capture, so the\n    envelope always parses and the node reports a clipped result instead of an error.\n    The property still worth guarding is that the cap is applied at all, which the\n    raised-cap test above pins from the other direction.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>With no cap threaded onto the plan (preview / eval-replay paths), the sandbox<br />\napplies its class default.</p>\n<pre><code>This previously asserted that the node *failed* on a &gt;64 KB output — because the\noversized value truncated the runner's JSON envelope. That was the C8 bounding\ndefect, not intended behaviour: the child now bounds its own capture, so the\nenvelope always parses and the node reports a clipped result instead of an error.\nThe property still worth guarding is that the cap is applied at all, which the\nraised-cap test above pins from the other direction.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789446489266,"stop":1789446489267,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_clear_prompt_info_cache